  "map_note": "The Morning Map's index cards are graded per session on their walls and flip level, not at these horizons, so they are not in the panels below: they are the rest of the published total.",
  "method": "Grades are recorded for each publishing day as a group, so a horizon's grade belongs to the day-group the record attaches it to, and is never split into a separate figure for each single call. A call is graded on the change from the closing price on the day it was published to the close 1, 5 and 21 trading days later. It counts as rose only if that change is above zero; flat counts with the ones that did not rise. Grades, once published, are never rewritten.",
